A single-line text field with optional icons, text or controls at either end, and a clear button.
[Appica docs](https://appica.dev/ui/components/react/input)

<%= embed UI::InputPreview, :default %>

## Usage

```ruby
Input(type: "email", placeholder: "you@example.com", aria_label: "Email")
Input(variant: :soft, size: :sm, start_slot: :search, clearable: true)
Input(start_slot: :mail, end_slot: "@example.com")
Input(end_slot: -> { Button(variant: :ghost, size: :sm, icon: true) { Icon(:eye) } })
```

A plain `Input` is a native `<input>` and takes any native attribute - `type`, `name`, `value`, `required`,
`pattern`, `aria_*`. As soon as it has a slot or `clearable:`, it sits in one bordered frame: `class:` styles the
frame and `input: { … }` reaches the inner `<input>`. Label it with a [Field](<%= page_path(:field) %>), a
`<label for>` or `aria_label:`.

