## API reference

| Prop | Type | Default | Description |
|------|------|---------|-------------|
| `variant:` | `:outline`, `:soft` | `:outline` | Bordered or filled. |
| `size:` | `:sm`, `:md`, `:lg` | `:md` | Height, padding and text size. |
| `start_slot:` / `end_slot:` | `Symbol`, `String`, `Proc` | - | Adornments: an icon name, text, or a block. |
| `clearable:` | `Boolean` | `false` | A ✕ that empties the field once it has a value. |
| `clear_label:` | `String` | "Clear input" | The clear button's accessible name (translated). |
| `invalid:` | `Boolean` | - | Paints the error state and sets `aria-invalid` (a Field sets it for you). |
| `input:` | `Hash` | `{}` | Attributes for the inner `<input>` when it's wrapped. |

Any other attribute goes to the `<input>` (`class:` to the frame when wrapped). Clearing dispatches `input` on the
field and `ui--input:clear` on the frame.

## Accessibility

- Give every input a label: a Field's `FieldLabel`, a `<label for>` or `aria_label:`.
- The clear button is a real `<button>` with a translated name; it appears only while there is a value and returns
  focus to the input.
- `invalid:` sets `aria-invalid="true"`; inside a Field the error is linked with `aria-describedby`.
